It REUSES, by reference, code that is itself derived from open-code-review
(https://github.com/alibaba/open-code-review), Copyright Alibaba Group,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0:

  source.js
      imports parseUnifiedDiff / hunkLineCounts / hunkNewSpan from
      ../code-review/source.js and delegates enumeration to it.
      <- open-code-review internal/diff/hunk.go (hunkHeaderRe) and
         internal/diff/parser.go, via domains/code-review/source.js.
      Deviation: none in the reused parser. What this domain adds is the
      `serviceMap` join onto `candidate.meta.service`; it does not change which
      candidates exist, their ids, their locators or the gate predicates that
      see them.

  anchor.js
      re-exports ../code-review/anchor.js unchanged (object identity; the
      domain's test asserts `anchor === codeReviewAnchor`).
      <- open-code-review internal/diff/resolver.go (normalizeLine,
         matchConsecutive, RelocateAcrossFiles). The same deviation documented
         in the root NOTICE for domains/code-review/anchor.js applies verbatim:
         upstream's third tier re-locates with a model call; this port stops at
         "unanchored" and distinguishes `locator-mismatch` from
         `relocation-ambiguous`.

  evidence.js
      spreads ../code-review/evidence.js's three tools into its toolkit by
      function identity, and adds `interface_delta`.
      <- the layout of internal/tool/file_read.go and internal/tool/git_grep.go
         (bounded read/search payloads) via domains/code-review/evidence.js.
      `interface_delta` is ORIGINAL to this project: a coarse, bounded scan of
      ADDED diff lines for declaration shapes. It is a locator, not a parser,
      and its own `provenance` string says so.

  index.js
      gate.extensions
      <- internal/config/allowlist/supported_file_types.json via
         domains/code-review/index.js. This list is a SMALL SUBSET of upstream's
         116 extensions (17 here, plus the extensions code-review already
         admits); it is NOT a full port and does not claim parity.

  rules/*.md
      Original prose written for this project. NOT derived from open-code-review
      and NOT expert-validated: every document carries
      `needs-expert-review: true`.

Everything else in this directory — the service-boundary join, the review
order, the rule library, `interface_delta`, the fixtures and the test suite —
is original to this project.

Note requested for the package-root NOTICE (this file is the domain-local
